; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; adjuncts.madj - the English edge adjuncts: the words a sentence may open or
; close with that carry no meaning the grammar reads, and the register each
; sets on what was said. Matched on TOKENS at the sentence's edges, only after
; the exact parse failed (an adjunct word can be content: "are you well"); a
; proper name set off by a comma at an edge is a vocative too and rides the
; /addressee rider.
;
; Format: `<phrase> <role> [<axis> [<value>]]`
;   role   discourse | vocative | politeness | protected
;   axis   tone warm-joy|cold-anger|anxious-fear|heavy-grief|proud|light
;          warmth hostile|cool|warm|fond
;          formality intimate|familiar|formal|deferential
;          confidentiality          (no value: the speaker asks for discretion)
;          authority                (no value: the speaker invokes office or law)
; A `protected` word is never stripped from an edge and never skipped by a
; relaxed reading: the negations, which turn a question's meaning over.
; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

; Politeness.
please              politeness   warmth warm
if you please       politeness   warmth warm
if you would        politeness   formality formal
if it please you    politeness   formality deferential
kindly              politeness   warmth warm
thank you           politeness   warmth warm
i beg your pardon   politeness   formality deferential
begging your pardon politeness   formality deferential

; Vocatives.
sir                 vocative     formality formal
madam               vocative     formality formal
ma'am               vocative     formality formal
mister              vocative     formality formal
your honour         vocative     formality deferential
your worship        vocative     formality deferential
my lord             vocative     formality deferential
my lady             vocative     formality deferential
officer             vocative     formality formal
constable           vocative     formality formal
inspector           vocative     formality formal
doctor              vocative     formality formal
father              vocative     formality formal
reverend            vocative     formality formal
friend              vocative     warmth warm
my friend           vocative     warmth fond
my dear             vocative     warmth fond
my good man         vocative     formality familiar
my good woman       vocative     formality familiar
mate                vocative     formality familiar
man                 vocative     formality familiar
you fool            vocative     warmth hostile
you dog             vocative     warmth hostile
you wretch          vocative     warmth hostile
you liar            vocative     warmth hostile

; Discourse markers.
well                discourse
now                 discourse
so                  discourse
then                discourse
say                 discourse
pray                discourse    formality formal
look here           discourse    formality familiar
oi                  discourse    formality familiar
hey                 discourse    formality familiar
come                discourse
come now            discourse
right               discourse
anyway              discourse
in confidence       discourse    confidentiality
between ourselves   discourse    confidentiality
in the name of the law discourse authority
by order of the court  discourse authority

; Protected: never stripped, never skipped.
not                 protected
no                  protected
never               protected
nor                 protected
neither             protected
nobody              protected
nothing             protected
none                protected
